Confirmed findings:
1. **P1 — abort cannot stop queued integrations (operation_runner.ts:185, 191; :383-401; :553-558; SPEC §3.5, §5.3, ACC-V11-GIT-04).** \`executeBatch\` awaits each \`execute\`, which itself awaits \`enqueueIntegration\`; only after the batch/queue settles does \`run\` call \`cancelled()\` and set operation status CANCELLED. The queue’s skip predicate checks that status, so queued work cannot observe cancellation in this path. The current MAO-08 test only has both fake executors resolve \`cancelled\` when signaled; it doesn’t include a completed unit with an integration waiting behind a batch-mate.
2. **P1 — message can be marked delivered without ever reaching the durable conversation (operation_runner.ts:173-185; operation_messages.ts:110-128; operation_runner_execution.ts:346-365, 496-504; SPEC §6.3.3).** Delivery is persisted before \`executeBatch\`; a crash before task binding/prompt leaves the message’s deliveredTo entry but no agent task. Resume recomputes undelivered messages, so \`initialPrompt\` gets none. Existing message tests only cover normal delivery/reconstruction.
3. **P1 — isolated TDD snapshot reads a shared mutable workspace (operation_runner_execution.ts:101, 270, 282-283, 389-394).** Parallel calls to one executor overwrite \`runWorkspace\`; after one unit awaits \`runTurn\`, its post-turn snapshot can hash changes from a batch-mate’s worktree. This can make TDD evidence/candidate identity belong to the wrong unit.
4. **P1 — an integrated unit recovered after a crash never publishes its completion message (operation_runner.ts:508-525; SPEC §6.3.2-6.3.4).** The receipt recovery sets status/result and emits WORK_COMPLETED, but does not call \`publishCompletion\`; downstream units then lack the artifact required as operator-visible summary/advisory context.
5. **P2 — inherited object keys pass role validation (operation_cli.ts:136-137; roles.ts:20-76).** \`role in ROLE_PROFILES\` accepts \`constructor\`, \`toString\`, etc. They are not supported roles; \`constructor\` reads as a role but isn’t in READ_ONLY_ROLES and has no role profile. Replace with an own-property/enum check. Current test only rejects \`wizard\`.
6. **P2 — operation schema gate runs after envelope protection/migration (operation_runner_persistence.ts:73-79; state.ts:608-610, 646-666; SPEC §4.2, VALIDATION.md future-version row).** An old build can redact/save a future operation record while loading its envelope, before \`migrateOperationState\` throws. This is conditional on the envelope migration/redaction changing the record; current test checks not-quarantined but not unchanged-on-disk. Test a future nested version plus a field that the current redactor would transform.

Not independently confirmed yet: batch execution buffers operation results until every promise settles (\`executeBatch\` lines 241-257; results applied/saved lines 185-190). The required real-kill MAO-07 is explicitly still owed and can establish whether a finished task replays tool work. Also, scheduler exceptions are not caught at \`scheduler.decide()\` (line 145), despite SPEC §3.5’s required NOT_CONVERGING block; please decide whether to include this in the fix set.

The exact candidate currently has no GitHub PR or hosted CI run. I observed two active local CLI suite runs on 853c6333; one has emitted an outer suite failure and neither has terminal aggregate results. Don’t treat them as accepted evidence. I did not run another suite due the active runners.

The detached review worktree is /home/mike/nexus-wt/v11-independent-review-20261031. I can review the post-fix exact head when available.`
